Then—from the short vow; Sheeradhwaja—Sheeradhwaja; Jajne—produced; Yagya-Artham—for performing Yagya; Karshata—while plowing the land;
Mahim—to the earth; Sita—Sita Devi, the wife of Ramachandra; Sheer-Agrahata—from the front part of the plow; Jata—produced; Tasmat—therefore;
Sheeradhwaja—Sheeradhwaja; Smrutah—became famous. Hrasvaroma produced a son named Shiradhwaja (whose name was also Janaka). When he was plowing the field,
a maiden named Sitadevi appeared from the front of his plow, who later became the wife of Lord
Ramachandra. In this way, he was called Shiradhwaj. Kushadhwajastasya putrastato dharmadhwajo nripa. Dharmadhvajasya dwau putraau kritadhvajamitadhvajau. 19. Meaning of the word

Kushadhwajah - Kushadhwaja; Tasya - His; Putrah - Son; Tatah - From him; Dharmadhwajah - Dharmadhwaja; Nripah - King; Dharmadhwajasya - Of Dharmadhwaja;
Dau - Two; Putrau - Son; Krutadhwaja-mitadhwajau - Krutadhwaja and Mitadhwaja..

Sheeradhwaj's son was Kushadhwaj, and Kushadhwaj's son was Raja Dharmadhwaj, who had two sons named Krutadhwaj
and Mitadhwaj.
Kritadhvajashtidhvajah, Khandikyaastu mitadhvajah. Kritadhvasuta rajannatmavidvisharada. 20>. Khandikya, the knower of the nature of action, was afraid, struck down by the Keshi flag. Bhanumantasya putro bhuuchatadyumnastu tatputra. 21). Meaning of the word

Krutadhvaja-putra—from Krutadhvaja; Keshi-dhvaja—Keshi-dhvaja; Khandikya—also the son named Khandikya; Mitadhvaja-putra—from Mitadhvaja;
Krutadhvaja-putra—son of Krutadhvaja; Rajan—Oh King; Atmavidya-visharadah—skilled in self-knowledge; Khandikya—Khandikya;
Karmatattva-vidnah—skilled in the Vedic rituals; Bhitah—fearing; Keshi-dhvaja—from Keshi-dhvaja; Drutah—fleeing; Bhanuman—Bhanuman;
Tasya—of Keshi-dhvaja; Putra—son; Abhut—was; Shatadyumna—Shatadyumna; Tu—but.

This is Maharaj Parikshit, the son of Kritadhwaja was Keshadhwaja, and the son of Mitadhwaja was Khandikya. Kritadhvaja had a son named Adrushta-Dhvaja, who was proficient in spiritual knowledge, and Mitadhvaja had a son named Vedic rituals. Khandikya fled in fear of Keshinadhva.
Keshidhwaja's son was Bhanuman, and Bhanuman's son
became Shatahruday. Shatadyumna happened. Shuchiṣṭu tanayastasmaṭasanadvājaḥ suto'bhabat. O energy-ketu, the son of Sanadvaja, the best of the Purujis. 22.

