If they are of equal level, then their meeting is praiseworthy. I consume ghee as my heroic food, and I do not desire anything else, except for intercourse. Vivasvanta, thus it is accepted, the great-minded. 22. Meaning of the word

Ghritam—Ghee or nectar; Me—Mine; Veera—Oh brave man; Bhakhyam—Edible item; Syat—Will be; Na—Not; Ikshe—I will see; Tva—To you;
Anyatra—At some other time; Maithunat—Except during the time of intercourse; Vivasasam—Naked, nude; Tat—That; Tatha Iti—Like this;
Pratipede—Given a promise; Mahamanah—The king Pururava. Urvashi said, "Hey Veer, I will only eat things made of ghee, and I would not want to see you naked at any other time besides the time of intercourse.""Vishalhridaya Pururava accepted these proposals. Oh! Beautiful, glorious, captivating to the world.
I will not serve you, O Manu, the goddess, you yourself have come. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word

Aho—amazing; Rupam—beauty; Aho—wonderful; Bhavah—expression, posture; Nar-loka—in human society or in the earthly realm; Vimohanam—so attractive; Kah—who; Na—not; Sevet—can accept; Manujah—human; Devim—to the goddess;
Tvam—like you; Swayam Agatam—coming on your own; Swagatam—welcome; Manujah—human; Devim—to the goddess;
