Tvam—like you; Swayam—on your own; Agatam—coming; Svagatam—welcome; Manujah—human; Devim—to the goddess;
Tvam—like you; Swayam—on your own; Agatam Pururava said: Oh beautiful woman, your beauty is wonderful and your expressions are also wonderful. Undoubtedly, you are a charm for all of humanity. Therefore, because you have come here voluntarily from the heavenly realm,
who on this earth would not be ready to serve a goddess like you? Meaning: It appears from Urvashi's words that the level of eating, living, conduct, and
speaking in the heavens is different from this earth. The inhabitants of heaven do not eat disgusting things like meat and eggs;
they only eat things made of ghee.
Nor do they wish to see men or women naked at any time other than the time of night. Being naked or nude is uncivilized, but nowadays in this world, being semi-nude
has become a fashion, and sometimes people like hippies stay completely naked. For this task,
